From 76f184529a31f00fdda695a03c0b39a9d992c76c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:53:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/25] Alerts, bot replies and notices in the reader's
 language
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Telegram chat in Slovak and a Discord server in English can share one
instance, so the language belongs to the destination, not the process: a
new `language` column (migration 0012), `--lang` on `destination`, a
selector per row in the dashboard, carried by export/import and by the
pairing so the bot answers in the chat's own language.

The machinery is gettext-shaped and deliberately not gettext: one JSON
catalog per language in `locales/`, `gettext`/`ngettext` with `{name}`
placeholders, English as the msgid so an untranslated string is never a
blank, and Slovak's three plural forms (1 / 2-4 / 5+) handled. No .po/.mo
compile step, nothing extra in the image, and Jinja's i18n extension can
take the same two callables when the UI follows.

Everything a destination reads is covered: listing alerts (price line,
market line, seller, buttons), price drops, verdict headlines and follow-
ups, digests, bot replies and /status, the block and stale notices, and
the Monday report. Status notices are now rendered per destination — the
dispatcher accepts a callable of the translator. Tests check that every
Slovak string keeps its placeholders and still corresponds to a string in
the code.

Found and fixed on the way: the 📊 market line added in 0017 was built but
never passed to the Telegram payload; it now is.
